77.m:
obeisance to Sūrya, to Bṛhaspati, to the Lord of Creatures (Prajāpati);
and to all the gods, and to all the Viśvedevas;
[Footnote]
1 "dattaṃ gṛhāṇa" is the reading of the two manuscripts marked ga and gha.
2 "anyārdham" is the reading of the manuscript marked kha; "antyārdham" is the reading of the manuscript marked ṅa.
3 "nidhānāyopakalpayet" is the reading of the two manuscripts marked ca and ṅa.
4 "hṛdi sthānamatikramet" is the reading of the manuscript marked ga;
"kādisthānamatikramāt" is the reading of the manuscript marked kha.
[Page 229]

78.m:
Īśvara said:
I shall explain the investiture with sacred thread (pavitrārohaṇa), which makes rites, worship, and the like complete;
it is designated as regular (nitya), and the other as occasional (naimittika).
